---
import PhotoPlaceholder from '../PhotoPlaceholder.astro';
import SectionHead from '../SectionHead.astro';
---

<section data-vision-section class="band-cream section">
  <SectionHead heading="What the doctors stop seeing." />

  <div class="container-page">
    <PhotoPlaceholder
      description="A family walking on a tree-shaded sidewalk — adults, kids, a stroller. Or a senior on a morning walk to a corner store. Daily activity built into daily life."
    />
  </div>

  <div class="container-narrow">
    <div class="vision-prose">
      <p>
        Walk to the store and you don't need to schedule gym time. Breathe cleaner air and your
        kid's inhaler goes unused for longer. Cross a street designed for people instead of
        forty-five-mile-per-hour cars and your neighbor doesn't end up in the trauma bay. Get
        outside to a park and you're not alone in your apartment all weekend. This is the piece of
        the vision nobody puts on the transit brochure, even though the research has said it for
        decades.
      </p>
      <p>
        The won Valley reduces the work doctors have to do. Asthma diagnoses drop because there are
        fewer bad-air days. Pediatric injury cases fall because cars don't hit children at the same
        speeds. Seniors stay less isolated because they can leave their houses without arranging a
        ride. Obesity-related conditions decline because daily activity is built into the commute
        instead of bolted onto the end of an exhausted day.
      </p>
      <p>
        Transit and walkable neighborhoods are the most cost-effective public-health tool a
        metropolitan area has. We just don't usually count the savings on the right side of the
        ledger.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
